    easy to access these things"): This PC and the navigation pane show
    "Drive mounts", the folder this account's drives are mounted in
    (/run/media/USER on Patrone, where USB drives appear), even while it's
    empty, and "Other mounts" (/mnt) when an administrator mounted
    something there. Each tile says what the folder is for and where.
  * Mount a shared folder from the Network page (the user: "Allow me to
    right click on a network folder and mount it"): a shared folder's
    right-click menu and the command bar have Mount and Map network drive,
    and a computer's has Map network drive with its address filled in as
    \\computer\. A computer or share has its own short menu (Open, Mount,
    Map network drive, Copy address), not a file's.
  * A network drive shows under This PC, in the navigation pane too, with
    the folder GVfs gives it (under /run/user), which every app can open, a
    terminal included; its address is in the tile's tooltip and
    Properties. Disconnect is in its menu in the navigation pane as well.
  * Map network drive puts the cursor after a filled-in address, and an
    address typed with spaces (\\nas\My Files) works.

