patrone-file-manager (0.3.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Drives and their mounts (the user, 2026-10-28: "add under computer
    Mounts where the drives are ... and add the ability to mount other
    drives/resources"). This PC lists every drive, mounted or not: each
    tile says where the drive is mounted ("Mounted at /run/media/..."),
    Linux's drive letter, and a drive that isn't mounted shows its size and
    "Not mounted". Opening it mounts it; so does Mount, in its right-click
    menu, the command bar and the navigation pane. Mounted drives have
    Eject (USB drives, discs, disk images) or Unmount (internal drives).
    Properties shows where a drive is mounted.
  * This PC and the navigation pane follow drives being mounted, plugged
    in and removed: they let go of GIO's volume monitor, and GIO freed it
    with the signals they had connected. The navigation pane no longer
    lists a drive twice when two of them change at once.
  * Map network drive, as on Windows, in place of Connect to server: a
    network folder's address (\\server\share, or sftp://, ftp://, dav://,
    nfs://), a sign-in if the server asks for one (the password can be
    remembered), and "Reconnect at sign-in". The address can be typed as
    soon as the dialog opens. Mapped drives stay in This PC's Network
    locations, by their own name and address, while disconnected, and
    connect again when opened and at each sign-in. Disconnect unmounts a
    network drive and forgets the mapping.
  * Disk images: right-click an .iso or .img file and choose Mount (also in
    the command bar). It's mounted read-only, as Windows does, and opens;
    a mounted .iso shows as a disc. Eject puts it away.
  * The package's preinst and postrm are executable.

