patrone-file-manager (0.2.10) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A name being typed (after Compress, New folder, New file or F2) is kept
    by a click anywhere else in the window or by switching windows, as on
    Windows; it had stayed open and highlighted. Esc still cancels.
  * A new ZIP or TAR file shows its icon, type and size at once: it is built
    under a hidden .NAME.part and given its name when finished.
  * A renamed or pasted item that sorts out of view is scrolled fully into
    view, not one row short.
  * Going back or up, by any route (Back, Up, the mouse's Back button,
    Alt+Left, Alt+Up, Backspace, the address bar or the folder tree),
    selects the folder you came out of, in view and with the keyboard
    focus, as on Windows.
  * The mouse's Back and Forward buttons work.
  * The selected part of a name being typed is drawn in the accent colour;
    it was faint.

