patrone-file-manager (0.2.8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * GNOME's Files (Nautilus) is retired without being removed: Ubuntu's
    session and GNOME's file dialogs for Snap and Flatpak apps need it.
    Its menu entry is replaced by a hidden one that opens no file types,
    and the org.freedesktop.FileManager1 D-Bus service ("show in folder")
    starts File Manager instead (--gapplication-service). Nautilus's own
    files are diverted to *.nautilus and come back when this package goes.
  * Open with no longer selects the first of "More apps" when nothing is
    suggested, and Always and Just once wait for an app to be picked;
    pressing Always had made Advanced Network Configuration the app for
    Flatpak files.
  * Home's Recent and Favorites columns line up with their headings.
  * No more "GFileInfo created without standard::content-type" warnings.

